From 0cda8e600c4a3d8067a6c4b42d2a679843f4646f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antoine Pichot <antoine.pichot@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:42:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] media: i2c: ov7251: Fix link frequency index

ov7251_check_hwcfg() looks for the first firmware link frequency the
driver supports, then stores the loop index into the firmware's
link_frequencies array (i) in link_freq_idx. That value is used as an
index into the driver's own link_freq[], pixel_rates[] and PLL1
configuration tables, so it has to be the index of the matching driver
entry (j).

The two only agree by chance. On the Microsoft Surface Book 2 the
endpoint built by ipu-bridge for the INT347E sensor lists a single link
frequency, 319.2 MHz (from the bridge's own per-sensor table, the ACPI
tables carry none): i is 0, so the driver selects link_freq[0],
programs the PLL for 240 MHz and
reports 240 MHz in V4L2_CID_LINK_FREQ and a 48 MHz pixel rate instead
of 319.2 MHz and 63.84 MHz.

Store j instead. On the Surface Book 2 the sensor then reports 319.2 MHz
and 63.84 MHz, and still streams at 30 fps through the IPU3 CIO2.

Fixes: cc125aaa5a78 ("media: i2c: Provide ov7251_check_hwcfg()")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Antoine Pichot <antoine.pichot@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c
index fce6344b51..1413f1856e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c
@@ -1523,7 +1523,7 @@ static int ov7251_check_hwcfg(struct ov7251 *ov7251)
 		goto out_free_bus_cfg;
 	}
 
-	ov7251->link_freq_idx = i;
+	ov7251->link_freq_idx = j;
 
 out_free_bus_cfg:
 	v4l2_fwnode_endpoint_free(&bus_cfg);
-- 
